  "job_B1.6.2.2_20251001_193254": {
    "text": "Nu synd twelf abusiua, \u00fe\u00e6t synd twelf un\u00feeawes \u00fee we eow secge\u00f0 on Leden & sy\u00f0\u00f0en on \u00e6nglisc.\nDuodecim abusiua sunt seculi, Hoc est, sapiens sine operibus bonis, senex sine religone, adolescens sine\nNu gyf se wyte by\u00f0 buten gode weorcan se \u00fee o\u00f0re mannen scolde syllen gode bisne, hwu ne by\u00f0 sone\nNe by\u00f0 se lare freomful, gyf se lar\u00f0eaw mid weorcan towurp\u00f0 his bodunge.\nEft gyf se lar\u00f0eaw dwele\u00f0, hwa by\u00f0 his lar\u00f0eaw sy\u00f0\u00f0en?\nGyf \u00fe\u00e6t eage ablinde\u00f0, ne by\u00f0 seo hand lochigende.\nSe ealde mann \u00fee by\u00f0 buten \u00e6wf\u00e6stnysse by\u00f0 \u00fean treowwe gelic, \u00fee leaf ber\u00f0 & blostmen, & n\u00e6nne\nHw\u00e6t by\u00f0 \u00e6fre swa stuntlic, swa \u00fe\u00e6t se ealde nelle his mod to Gode gew\u00e6nden mid goden ingehyde,\nJunge mannen m\u00e6ig tweonigen hwe\u00f0er heo moten libben, & se ealde m\u00e6ig wyten gewiss him \u00feone\n\u00dean ealden is to warnigen wi\u00f0 \u00fea yfele ge\u00f0ohtes, for\u00fean \u00fee seo heorte ne ealde\u00f0, ne eac seo tunge, ac\nWyte for \u00fey se ealde hw\u00e6t his elde gedafenige, & \u00fea \u00feing forseo \u00fee his sawle derige\u00f0.\nSe \u00feridde un\u00f0eaw is on \u00feyssen wurlde, \u00fe\u00e6t se junge mann beo buten gehersumnysse.\nUnwur\u00f0 by\u00f0 se on elde \u00fe\u00e6t him o\u00f0re m\u00e6nn \u00feenigen, se \u00fee on jugo\u00f0e nele his eldren gehersumigen.\nUre H\u00e6lend on his jugo\u00f0e w\u00e6s gehyrsum his magen, & his Heofonlice F\u00e6der he gehyrsumode o\u00f0 dea\u00f0.\nSwa swa \u00fean ealden gedafonige\u00f0 dugende \u00feeawes & geripode syfernysse, swa gerist \u00fean jungan \u00fe\u00e6t he\nGodes \u00e6 beot eac \u00fe\u00e6t mann arwur\u00f0ige symle his f\u00e6der & moder mid mycelre under\u00f0eodnysse, & gyf\nSe feor\u00f0e un\u00f0eaw is, \u00fe\u00e6t se welige mann beo buten \u00e6lmesd\u00e6den, & bedigelige his feoh, & geornlice\nUnges\u00e6lig by\u00f0 se gitsere, \u00fee \u00feurh his ges\u00e6l\u00f0e losa\u00f0, & for \u00fean gewitegendlice \u00feingan forwur\u00f0 a on\n& ges\u00e6lige by\u00f0 symle \u00fea mildheorte, for \u00fean \u00fee heo gemete\u00f0 \u00fea mildheortnysse eft.\nSe \u00fee d\u00e6l\u00f0 \u00e6lmesse for his Drihtenes lufen, se behytt his goldhord on heofone rice, \u00fe\u00e6r nan scea\u00f0e ne\nOn manegan \u00feingen man m\u00e6ig wyrcen \u00e6lmessen, on \u00e6te & on w\u00e6te & on gew\u00e6den eac & on\nEalle \u00feiss by\u00f0 \u00e6lmesse, & eac \u00fe\u00e6t mann beswinge \u00feone stunten for steore, se \u00fee steren sceal, for\u00fean \u00fee\nNe licge on \u00feine horde, \u00fe\u00e6t \u00fean hafeleasen m\u00e6ig freomigen to bigwisten, for\u00fean \u00fee \u00feu ne brucst ane\n\u00deu gaderest ma & ma & m\u00e6n cwele\u00f0 hungre, & \u00feine welen forrotige\u00f0 \u00e6tforen \u00feinen eagen.\nDo\u00f0 swa swa Drihten cw\u00e6\u00f0, D\u00e6le\u00f0 \u00e6lmessen & ealle \u00feing eow by\u00f0 cl\u00e6ne, \u00feiss he cw\u00e6\u00f0 on his\nSe fifte un\u00f0eaw is, \u00fe\u00e6t wif beo unseodefull.\nUnseodefull by\u00f0 scame for wurlde, & \u00fe\u00e6t unsedefulle wif by\u00f0 unwur\u00f0 on life, & eft \u00e6fter life nan\nWisedom gerist weren & wifen sydefullnysse, for \u00fean seo sydefullnysse gescylt heo wi\u00f0 un\u00f0eawes.\n\u00de\u00e6r \u00fe\u00e6r seo seodefullnysse by\u00f0, \u00fe\u00e6r by\u00f0 eac cl\u00e6nnysse, & \u00fe\u00e6t seodefulle wif onscune\u00f0 gittsunge &\nHeo heo warne\u00f0 wi\u00f0 druncannysse & wordlunge ne lufe\u00f0.\nWitodlice seo sydefullnysse gewyllt ealle un\u00f0eawes, & gode \u00feeawes heo healt \u00fee Gode lichige\u00f0 &\nSe sixte un\u00f0eaw is, \u00fe\u00e6t se \u00fee to hlaforde beo gesett, \u00fe\u00e6t for modeleaste ne muge his mannen don\nSume hlafordes geneal\u00e6ce\u00f0 \u00feurh heora hlafordscipe to Gode, swa swa Moyses se arwur\u00f0e, \u00fee to \u00fean\nSe hlaford sceal beon li\u00f0e \u00fean goden & egefull \u00fean dysigen, \u00fe\u00e6t he heora dysig alecge, & he sceal beon\nElles ne by\u00f0 his gefadung ne f\u00e6st ne langsum.\nHe sceal beon swa geworht, \u00fe\u00e6t him wi\u00f0 mote specan, & swa hw\u00e6t swa he wreca, wreca for\nHit is gewriten on bocan, \u00fe\u00e6t se by\u00f0 eall swa scyldig, se \u00fee \u00fe\u00e6t yfel ge\u00f0afo\u00f0, swa swa se \u00fee hit de\u00f0,\nHe sceal hine ge\u00f0eodan mid \u00feeawf\u00e6stnysse to Gode, for \u00fean \u00fee he nane mihte habben, ne m\u00e6ig to rihte\nSe hlaford sceal hogien \u00fe\u00e6t he habbe Godes fylst, & he ortuwigen ne sceal ahwar beo Godes fultume.\nGyf God by\u00f0 his gefylste, ne by\u00f0 his mihte forseowen, for \u00fean \u00fee nan mihte nis buten of Gode, se \u00fee\nHe awyrp\u00fe \u00fea modige of heora mihtesetle, & ahef\u00f0 \u00fea eadmede, \u00fe\u00e6t eall middeneard beo Gode\nSe seofo\u00f0e un\u00f0eaw is \u00fe\u00e6t se cristene man beo sacfull.\nOf Cristes name is christianus gehaten, \u00fe\u00e6t is se cristene mann, \u00fee on Criste is gefulhtod.\nGyf he \u00feonne by\u00f0 sacfull, ne by\u00f0 he so\u00f0lice cristene.\nNis nan mann so\u00f0lice cristen, bute se \u00fee Criste geefenl\u00e6ce\u00f0.\nCrist sylf nolde fliten, swa swa his F\u00e6der cw\u00e6\u00f0 beo him, Efne her is min cild \u00fee me is swy\u00f0e leof, &\nNe flitt he mid ceaste, ne saca ne astyre\u00f0, ne on str\u00e6te ne gehyr\u00f0 \u00e6nig mann his st\u00e6mne.\nHe cw\u00e6\u00f0 eac on his godspelle, \u00fe\u00e6t \u00fea by\u00f0 Godes bearn, \u00fea \u00fee gesibsume by\u00f0, & saca ne astyrige\u00f0.\nSwa swa \u00fea gesibsume so\u00f0lice Godes bearn by\u00f0, swa by\u00f0 eac \u00fea sacfulle so\u00f0lice deofles bearn.\nEalle we clypige\u00f0 to Gode & cwe\u00f0e\u00f0, Pater noster, \u00feu ure f\u00e6der \u00fee eart on heofone.\nAc we ne mugen habben \u00feone heofonlice e\u00f0el bute we fram eallen sacan orsorge beon.\nSe ehte\u00f0e un\u00f0eaw is, \u00fe\u00e6t se \u00feearefe beo modig.\nManig mann n\u00e6fe\u00f0 \u00e6hte, & hafe\u00f0 modignysse swa \u00feeh, & is earm for wurlde & unges\u00e6lig for Gode,\nCrist cw\u00e6\u00f0 on his godspelle beo \u00fean gastlice \u00feearfen, Beati pauperes spiritu quoniam ipsorum est\n\u00dea by\u00f0 \u00feearfe on gaste, \u00fea \u00fea for Godes lufe by\u00f0 eadmode, for\u00fean \u00fee \u00fe\u00e6s modes eadmodnysse m\u00e6ig\nWitodlice \u00fea rice, \u00fee rihtlice libbe\u00f0 mugen beon getealde betwux Godes \u00feearfen, gyf heo\nSe modige \u00feearfe, for his modes upahafennysse, is to ricen geteald rihtlice on bocan, & se eadmode\nSe nigo\u00f0e un\u00f0eaw is, \u00fe\u00e6t se cyng beo unrihtwis.\nSe cyng by\u00f0 gecoren to \u00fean \u00fee him cy\u00f0\u00f0 his name.\nRex we cwe\u00f0e\u00f0 cyng, \u00fe\u00e6t is gecwe\u00f0en Wissigend, for\u00fean \u00fee he sceal wissigen mid wisedome his\n\u00de\u00e6s cynges rihtwisnysse ar\u00e6r\u00f0 his cynesetle, & \u00fe\u00e6s folcas steora gesta\u00f0ele\u00f0 his so\u00f0f\u00e6stnysse.\n\u00de\u00e6t is cynges rihtwisnysse \u00fe\u00e6t he mid riccetre ne ofsitte, ne earmne ne eadigne, ac \u00e6lcen deme riht.\nHe sceal beon bewerigend wydewena & steopcildena, & stale alecgen, & forliger gewitnigen, & \u00fea\nWeotan him sculen r\u00e6den & he ne sceal beon weamod.\nGodes mynster he sceal myndigen \u00e6fre, & feden \u00feearfe, & f\u00e6stlice winnen wi\u00f0 onsigendne here, &\nHe sceal so\u00f0f\u00e6ste m\u00e6nn setten him to gerefen, & for Gode libben his lif rihtlice, & beon earfo\u00f0 on\nHe sceal hine gebiddan on gesetten timen, & \u00e6r m\u00e6ltime metes ne onbyrigen.\nFor\u00fean \u00fee hit is awriten, \u00fe\u00e6t wa \u00fe\u00e6re \u00feeode \u00fe\u00e6r se cyng by\u00f0 cild, & \u00fe\u00e6r \u00fea ealdorm\u00e6nn ete\u00f0 on\nGyf se cyng wyle mid carfullnysse healden \u00fea fores\u00e6de beboden, \u00feonne by\u00f0 his rice gesundfull on\nGyf he \u00feonne forsih\u00f0 \u00feas gesettnysse & lare, \u00feonne by\u00f0 his eard gehearemed foroft, \u00e6ig\u00f0er gea on\nWyte eac se cyng hwu hit is gecwe\u00f0en on bocan gyf he rihtwisnysse ne healt, \u00fe\u00e6t swa swa he ahafen\nSe teo\u00f0e un\u00f0eaw is, \u00fe\u00e6t se biscop beo gemeleas.\nEpiscopus is Grechisc name, \u00fe\u00e6t is on Leden Speculator, & on \u00e6nglisc Sceawere, for\u00fean \u00fee he is\nGyf \u00feu \u00fean arleasen nelt his arleasnysse asecgen, \u00feonne swelt se arlease on his arleasnysse, & ic ofga\nGyf \u00feu \u00feonne warnest \u00feone arlease were, & he nylle gecyrren fram his synnen \u00feurh \u00fee, he swylt on\nGyf se biscop beo gemeleas \u00feonne he Godes bydel is, & to lar\u00f0eawe gesett \u00fean l\u00e6weden folca, \u00feonne\nSe \u00e6ndlyfte un\u00f0eaw is, \u00fe\u00e6t folc beo buten steore.\nFeale by\u00f0 stuntnyssen, \u00fe\u00e6r \u00fe\u00e6r nan steore ne by\u00f0, & \u00fe\u00e6r \u00fe\u00e6t dysig by\u00f0 orsorh, & \u00fe\u00e6t gedwyld rixe\u00f0,\nBeo \u00fean cw\u00e6\u00f0 se sealmwyrhte \u00feysen worden clypigende, Apprehendite disciplinam nequando\nEac Paulus se apostol cw\u00e6\u00f0 on his pistole, \u00feurhwunige\u00f0 on steora, & gewitodlice by\u00f0 swylce\nEft se witega Ysaias be \u00fean ilcan cw\u00e6\u00f0, Quiescite agere peruerse, discite bene facere, Geswica\u00f0\nDauid cw\u00e6\u00f0 eac, Declina a malo & fac bonum, Buh fram yfele & do god.\nGyf \u00feu unsc\u00e6\u00f0\u00f0ig seo, gescild \u00fee wi\u00f0 yfel, & gyf \u00feu sc\u00e6\u00f0\u00f0ig w\u00e6re, gew\u00e6nd \u00fee fram yfele, \u00feel\u00e6ste\nSe twelfte un\u00f0eaw is, \u00fe\u00e6t folc beo buten \u00e6.\nWe ne moten nu healden Moyses \u00e6 on \u00fean ealde wisen \u00e6fter ures H\u00e6lendes tocyme, ac we scylen\nManege weges synd swa swa se wisedom clype\u00f0.\n\u00dee mannen \u00feynce\u00f0 rihte, ac heo swa \u00feeh gel\u00e6de\u00f0 to dea\u00f0e on \u00e6nde, \u00fea \u00fea him dyselice folgige\u00f0.\nSe \u00fee Godes \u00e6 forl\u00e6tt, seo \u00fee is ure weig, se sceal mistlice faren on manegan gedwylden.\nCrist sylf is se weig, swa swa he s\u00e6de beo him, Ego sum uia & ueritas & uita, Ic sylf eam se weig &\nAc we by\u00f0 \u00feurh Crist to heofone gebrohte, gyf we his biggenges healde\u00f0.\n\u00dea \u00fea buten Godes \u00e6 & Godes gesetnysse libbe\u00f0, \u00fea by\u00f0 buten Gode \u00e6fre wunigende.\nDrihten sylf behet \u00feiss \u00fean \u00fee healde\u00f0 his beboden, Ecce ego uobiscum sum omnibus diebus, usque ad\nSe H\u00e6lend us gewissige to his wille symle, \u00fe\u00e6t ure sawlen moten si\u00f0igen eft to him \u00e6fter ure life, to\nSy him a wuldor & wur\u00f0mynt, Amen.\nNu syndon ehte heafodlehtres \u00fee us onwinne\u00f0 swy\u00f0e.\nAn is gecwe\u00f0en gula, \u00fe\u00e6t is gifernysse on \u00e6nglisc.\nSeo de\u00f0 \u00fe\u00e6t mann ett \u00e6rtime & drinc\u00f0, o\u00f0\u00f0e he eft to mycel nym\u00f0 on \u00e6te o\u00f0\u00f0e on wiste, seo forde\u00f0\nHe forde\u00f0 eac \u00fea sawle, for \u00fean \u00fee he sceal synegian oft, \u00feone he sylf nat hwu he f\u00e6r\u00f0 for his\nSe o\u00f0er lehter is forleger, & ungemetegod galnysse.\nSe is gehaten fornicatio, & he befyl\u00f0 \u00feone mann, & maca\u00f0 of Cristes lymen myltestrena lymen, & of\nSe \u00feridde is auaritia, \u00fe\u00e6t is seo yfele gitsung, & seo is wyrttrume \u00e6lcere wohnysse, heo maca\u00f0 reaflac\nSe feor\u00f0e lehter is ira, \u00fe\u00e6t is on \u00e6nglisc weamodnysse, se de\u00f0 \u00fe\u00e6t se mann nah his modes geweald, ac\nSe fifte is tristicia, \u00fe\u00e6t is \u00feysser wurlde unrotnysse, \u00feone se mann geunrotso\u00f0 ealles to swy\u00f0e for his\nTwa unrotnysse synd, an is \u00feeos yfele, & o\u00f0er is halwende, \u00fe\u00e6t man for his synnen geunrotsige.\nSe sixte lehter is accidia gehaten, \u00fe\u00e6t is asolcannysse o\u00f0\u00f0e sl\u00e6w\u00f0e on \u00e6nglisc, \u00feonne \u00fean m\u00e6nn ne\nSe seofo\u00f0e lehter is jactantia, \u00fe\u00e6t is idelgelp on Engliscre sp\u00e6ce, \u00feonne se mann by\u00f0 lofgeorn & mid\nSe ehte\u00f0e lehter is superbia gehaten, \u00fe\u00e6t is on Englisc modignysse gecweden.\nSeo is ord & \u00e6nde \u00e6lcere synne, seo geworhte \u00e6ngles to atelicen deoflen, & \u00feone mann maca\u00f0 eac,\nNu synden ehte heafodm\u00e6gna, \u00fea mugen oferswi\u00f0en \u00fea fores\u00e6de deoflen, \u00feurh Drihtenes fylste.\nAn is Temperantia, \u00fe\u00e6t is gemetegung on \u00e6nglisc, \u00fe\u00e6t man beo gemetegod, & to mycel ne \u00feygge on\nNytene eta\u00f0 swa \u00e6r swa heo hit habbe\u00f0, ac se gescadwise mann sceal chepen his m\u00e6les, & \u00feonne mid\nSeo o\u00f0er mihte is Castitas, \u00fe\u00e6t is cl\u00e6nnysse on \u00e6nglisc, \u00fe\u00e6t se l\u00e6wede hine healde buten forligere on\nSeo \u00feridde mihte is Largitas, \u00fe\u00e6t is cystignysse on \u00e6nglisc, \u00fe\u00e6t mann wislice aspende, na for\nGod nyle \u00fe\u00e6t we beon gr\u00e6dige gitseres, ne eac for wurldgelpe forwurpen ure \u00e6hte, ac d\u00e6len heo mid\nSeo feor\u00f0e mihte is Pacientia, \u00fe\u00e6t is ge\u00f0yld gecwe\u00f0en, \u00fe\u00e6t se man beo ge\u00f0yldig & \u00feolemod for Gode,\nSe heofonlice wisedom cw\u00e6\u00f0, \u00fe\u00e6t yrre h\u00e6f\u00f0 wununge on \u00fe\u00e6s dysigen bosme, \u00feonne he by\u00f0 to\nSeo fifte mihte is Spiritalis leticia, \u00fe\u00e6t is seo gastlice blisse, \u00fe\u00e6t man on Gode blissige betwux\n\u00deider we sculen efstan of \u00feysser earfo\u00f0nysse mid gastlicre blisse, \u00feonne by\u00f0 seo unrotnysse mid eallen\nSeo sixte mihte is Instantia boni operis, \u00fe\u00e6t is anr\u00e6dnysse godes weorcas.\nGyf we by\u00f0 anr\u00e6de on uren gode weorcan, \u00feonne muge we oferswi\u00f0en \u00fea asolcannysse, swa for \u00fean\nSeo seofo\u00f0e mihte is seo so\u00f0e lufe to Gode, \u00fe\u00e6t we on gode weorcan Godes lufe cepen, na ideles\nAc uten don \u00e6lmesse swa swa he us t\u00e6hte, Gode to lofe, na us to hlysan, \u00fe\u00e6t God sy geherod on uren\nSeo ehte\u00f0e mihte is seo so\u00f0e eadmodnysse, gea to Gode gea to mannen, mid modes hlutternysse, for\nOn hwan m\u00e6ig se man modegien \u00feeh he wylle, ne m\u00e6ig he on ge\u00f0ing\u00f0en, for \u00fean \u00fee feala synd\nNe m\u00e6ig he on his \u00e6hte, for \u00fean \u00fee he his \u00e6nded\u00e6ig nat, ne on nane \u00feingan he ne m\u00e6ig modegigen\nNu ge habbe\u00f0 geherd hwu \u00feas halge m\u00e6gn oferswi\u00f0e\u00f0 \u00fea lehtres, \u00fee deofol besaw\u00f0 on us, & gyf we\nWe mugen \u00feurh Godes fylst \u00fea feondlice lehtres mid gecampe oferwinnen gyf we chenlice fihte\u00f0, &",
